    14	Removing the depth bound from the second command makes the LLVM interpreter
    15	exit 113 when it is asked to evaluate the deliberately opaque function.  The
    16	Haskell proof does not approximate that call: it proves for every nonempty
    17	symbolic code sequence `CS` that the implementation returns exactly the
    18	reference value `str(md5hexCodes(CS))`.  A separate claim proves the empty
    19	sequence returns `noneV`.
