The translator check is byte-identical, so the proof is tied to the submitted `.mpy` artifact at that layer. The independent differential found a real implementation mismatch: all tested ASCII strings agree, but every tested non-ASCII string raises `UnicodeEncodeError` in the trusted canonical (`encode("ascii")`) while the candidate returns a UTF-8 digest. I’ll still complete the proof reconstruction and static soundness audit; this divergence will be judged separately from whether the K claims themselves close.
