codex
The false-postcondition check is also clean: the mutated spec builds (`--dry-run`, exit 0), then fails with `WarnStuckClaimState` because execution yields `str(md5hexCodes([97]))` while the mutation demands `None`. So the original claims are result-constraining and non-vacuous; the final negative verdict rests on real-program fidelity and semantic unsoundness, not on failure to reconstruct or discriminate the proof.
